const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先限定问题：便宜的股票并不相同",en:"Cheap stocks are not interchangeable"},body:{zh:"Piotroski从高账面市值比股票出发，研究财务报表能否区分其中经营状况较强与较弱的企业。这里的财务信号服务于一个已经限定的价值股样本，并不是先给全市场公司打分，再声称同一阈值适合所有行业、规模和市场。",en:"Piotroski starts with high book-to-market stocks and asks whether financial statements distinguish stronger from weaker firms within that group. The accounting signals address a bounded value-stock sample. They do not establish that a single score threshold applies to every industry, company size or market."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第2, 5–7页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 2, 5–7"}}},{title:{zh:"盈利与现金流要一起看",en:"Read profitability alongside cash flow"},body:{zh:"盈利组包含四项信号：资产收益为正、经营现金流为正、资产收益改善，以及现金流高于会计利润。利润和现金流使用期初资产缩放；最后一项关注应计成分。只保留净利润是否增长，会丢失现金支持程度与资产规模这两层信息。",en:"Four profitability signals cover positive return on assets, positive operating cash flow, improving return on assets and cash flow exceeding accounting earnings. Earnings and cash flow are scaled by beginning assets; their comparison captures accruals. Earnings growth alone loses both cash support and the asset base underlying profitability."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第7–8页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 7–8"}}},{title:{zh:"融资状态与经营效率是另外两组",en:"Financing and operations supply five more signals"},body:{zh:"另五项分别观察长期杠杆下降、流动比率改善、没有发行普通股，以及毛利率和资产周转率改善。毛利率的分母是销售额，周转率则连接销售与资产。它们描述不同变化，不能用一个名称宽泛的“盈利能力”字段替代。",en:"Five further signals track lower long-term leverage, improving current ratio, no common-equity issuance, improving gross margin and improving asset turnover. Gross margin uses sales as its denominator, whereas turnover links sales to assets. These are distinct changes, not interchangeable versions of a generic profitability field."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第8–10页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 8–10"}}},{title:{zh:"九个判断，不是精确的经营刻度",en:"Nine binary judgements, not a continuous scale"},body:{zh:"每项条件满足得一分，合计形成0至9的分数。这样的等权二元表达便于比较，却不保留改善幅度：略有改善与大幅改善可能同得一分。阅读时应保留原始财务值、比较期间和信号方向，避免把一分差异解释成固定的经济距离。",en:"Each satisfied condition contributes one point to a score from zero to nine. Equal-weight binary coding is easy to compare but discards magnitude: slight and substantial improvements can receive the same point. Preserve the underlying financial values, comparison periods and signal directions rather than treating each point as a fixed economic distance."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第7–10页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 7–10"}}},{title:{zh:"报告期末不是信息可用时点",en:"Respect the gap between fiscal year and use"},body:{zh:"研究样本覆盖1976至1996年，并在每个财政年度结束后的第五个月开始计算持有期收益。高账面市值比的样本筛选也需要财务资料齐备。这个历史时滞不证明其他市场的披露已经完成；实际应用仍要保留公告日期和修订版本。",en:"The sample covers 1976–1996, with holding-period returns beginning in the fifth month after fiscal year-end. High book-to-market selection also requires sufficient accounting data. This historical lag is not proof that disclosure is complete elsewhere; actual publication dates and revised filing versions remain essential for a new dataset."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第11–12页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 11–12"}}},{title:{zh:"结果也受样本退出规则影响",en:"Exits and exclusions affect interpretation"},body:{zh:"论文比较强弱财务组及整个高账面市值比样本，并使用不同统计检验。它在此处采用退市收益为零的假设，这会影响退出样本的处理。重读结果时，应把样本剔除、退市回报和缺失值规则一起考虑，不能只沿用评分而忽略收益序列如何形成。",en:"The paper compares financially stronger and weaker groups with the wider high book-to-market sample using multiple statistical tests. Its stated convention assumes a zero delisting return. Interpretation therefore needs exclusions, delisting treatment and missing-data rules alongside the score, rather than borrowing the signals while ignoring construction of the return series."},reference:{url:"https://www.ivey.uwo.ca/media/3775523/value_investing_the_use_of_historical_financial_statement_information.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2000年论文，第11–12页",en:"Source: 2000 paper, pp. 11–12"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"原研究针对历史高账面市值比股票。九项二元信号不是通用质量评级或买卖建议；样本时滞和退市处理会影响结果，迁移时需重新核对。",en:"The historical study concerns high book-to-market stocks. Nine binary signals are not a universal quality rating or a trading recommendation; availability lags and delisting treatment require renewed scrutiny in another sample."}};export{e as default};
